## Context
Two author directives from reading 1, both about anticipating referee attacks
on the experimental protocol.

## Actions
1. **Annex B verbatim prompt**: verify which prompt the rerun actually used
   (author believes the complete prompt — check the code), and reproduce it
   verbatim in Annex B. Annex B should also acknowledge two known prompt
   weaknesses: (a) we missed the "Start your answer with…" trick that would
   have simplified downstream parsing; (b) the status-list mismatch with the
   reference vocabulary (cf. "Proposed" stratum, 0534 item 1) — if confirmed,
   grounds for a rerun in the journal version.
2. **De-mine "why not tell the model to merge Wikipedia and GEM?"**: add prose
   answering the inevitable reviewer question. Since we want a GENERIC asset
   inventory method, we cannot provide the answer in the question — the model
   gets a fair chance: it has training data; in multi-turn we encourage source
   discovery. And we never disclose that the reference list is published on
   Zenodo.

## Relevant files
- `slides/manuscript/` — Annex B, §Exp1/Exp2 protocol prose
- `experiments/` — rerun prompt assembly code (verify which prompt shipped)

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Annex B contains the verbatim rerun prompt, verified against code.
- [ ] Annex B acknowledges the two prompt-design limitations.
- [ ] The merge-the-sources de-mining paragraph is in the protocol prose.
